+Exporting and importing JSON
+............................
+
+For a wholesale copy you can serialize an entire database with
+:meth:`~tinydb.database.TinyDB.export_json`. It returns a JSON string of every
+table, preserving each document's ID, so it can be fed straight into
+:meth:`~tinydb.database.TinyDB.import_json`:
+
+>>> from tinydb import TinyDB
+>>> db1 = TinyDB('db1.json')
+>>> db2 = TinyDB('db2.json')
+>>> db1.insert({'name': 'John', 'age': 22})
+1
+>>> data = db1.export_json()
+>>> db2.import_json(data)
+
+``import_json`` replaces the target database with the imported data. It
+validates the complete JSON object before writing anything, only accepts
+positive integer document IDs, and resets the target's table caches and
+next-ID allocation after a successful import. Invalid input raises
+``ValueError`` and leaves the existing database untouched.
+
